<div class="bb-quote">Quote:<br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">(2) Quite often the thing that kills CC&#39;s constructs are AOE damage, so you don&#39;t get to replace a construct as soon as it is destroyed. &nbsp;If you have a villain doing (ex:) 4 points of AOE damage, then any new construct will be killed as soon as it is put into play.
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
Since PW CC can react to construct destruction, he can damage and hopefully destroy whatever is dealing the AOE damage before it can damage other party members (kinda like Chrono-Ranger&#39;s Ultimate Target, or ExPat&#39;s HairTrigger Reflexes).If he can&#39;t, then I would use this opportunity to just draw cards and find the cards/constructs you need. &nbsp;If you have in hand a construct you don&#39;t need, you can play it, let it get destroyed and draw a new card. &nbsp;I actually find PW CC more likely to get the constructs I want because of this.I agree that if your constructs aren&#39;t getting destroyed then it&#39;s less effective. &nbsp;But if they aren&#39;t getting destroyed, for me that usually means the heroes are having a good game and are in control of things :)&nbsp;

[/quote]

You could always destroy one yourself to start the chain.
